{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Resurgence.StokesMatrixDescent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Resurgence.StokesMatrixDescent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.stokes_trace_block_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.stokes_trace_block_sum","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesMatrixDescent.lean#L106-L114","doc":"**`tr_M(S) = ∑_λ tr(e_λ S e_λ)`.**  Combining block-diagonalisation with\nadditivity of the matrix trace: the gauge-invariant Markov trace of an\nequivariant Stokes matrix decomposes as the sum of its per-partition block\ntraces.  Proved sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.stokes_block_diagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.stokes_block_diagonal","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesMatrixDescent.lean#L79-L95","doc":"**Block-diagonalisation (A.i).**  An `Sₙ`/Wedderburn-equivariant Stokes\nmatrix `S` is block-diagonal in the Young/Hecke idempotent decomposition:\n`S = ∑_λ e_λ S e_λ`.  Fully **proved** from completeness + off-block vanishing;\nno `sorry`, no axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.offblock_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.offblock_zero","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesMatrixDescent.lean#L68-L77","doc":"**Off-block vanishing.**  Under equivariance, the `(i,j)`-block `e_i S e_j`\nof an equivariant `S` vanishes for `i ≠ j`.  Proof: push `e_j` left through\n`S`, then use orthogonality `e_i e_j = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.CommutesFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.CommutesFamily","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesMatrixDescent.lean#L63-L66","doc":"**`Sₙ`/Wedderburn equivariance**: the Stokes matrix `S` commutes with every\nidempotent `e_λ` (equivalently, it commutes with the Young symmetrisers, i.e.\nis `Sₙ`-equivariant on the multiplicity spaces). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.IdempotentFamily.complete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.IdempotentFamily.complete","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesMatrixDescent.lean#L61-L61","doc":"The family is complete: `∑_i e_i = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.IdempotentFamily.ortho","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.IdempotentFamily.ortho","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesMatrixDescent.lean#L59-L59","doc":"Distinct idempotents are orthogonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.IdempotentFamily.idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.IdempotentFamily.idem","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesMatrixDescent.lean#L57-L57","doc":"Each `e_i` is idempotent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.IdempotentFamily.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.IdempotentFamily.mk","kind":"ctor","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesMatrixDescent.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.IdempotentFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.IdempotentFamily","kind":"structure","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesMatrixDescent.lean#L53-L61","doc":"A **complete orthogonal idempotent family** — the central Wedderburn /\nYoung idempotents `e_λ` of `H_n(q)`, one per partition `λ : ι`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Resurgence.stokes_trace_conj_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Resurgence.stokes_trace_conj_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Resurgence/StokesMatrixDescent.lean#L30-L39","doc":"**Stokes-trace descent (A.ii).**  A gauge / basis change acts on the\nStokes matrix by conjugation `S ↦ g S g⁻¹`; the bar-invariant, gauge-invariant\nobservable is the trace, a conjugacy invariant:\n`tr(g S g⁻¹) = tr(S)`.  This is the matrix-level Markov trace `tr_M(S)`, and it\nis **independent of the gauge `g`** — proved from trace cyclicity.  (The\nindependence of the *archimedean summation choice*, median vs lateral, is a\nseparate `ℝ`-level statement and is not part of this generic-ring scaffold.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}